WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.890
more than 300 ads for Donald Trump's reelection
campaign have been rejected by YouTube and

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:09.540
Google, and it is a fascinating situation
and one that was miserable.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.540
It's reported

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.540
to begin with.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.130
There were a whole bunch of headlines floating
around, which made it appear as though these

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:19.300
were Trump ads that had been pulled down.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.850
But the truth is these were never approved
to begin with and it does change our interpretation

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.850
of this.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:29.030
So we've talked before about how Donald Trump's
behavior on Twitter does seem to violate Twitter's

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:32.110
own terms and conditions because he's bullying
people.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:35.090
He's causing dog piling and targeted harassment.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.910
There's a really good case to be made that
Donald Trump's Twitter account should be banned,

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.330
but it hasn't been in the last few months.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:46.850
I've been getting more and more emails from
viewers saying, you know, David, before your

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.130
videos on YouTube, I'm seeing a Trump ad.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:56.580
And the ad is often riddled with lies or it's
attacking individuals in that seems to go

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.850
against YouTube's rules or whatever.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:02.760
And of course I always explained we don't
have any control over the ads, but that people

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:07.430
can report them to YouTube if they believe
that the ads violate the terms and conditions.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:12.820
We then heard from YouTube CEO Susan was Vicky
was risky.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.840
I completely, uh, I continue not to understand
how it's pronounced with just ski, but I guess

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.110
that's how she pronounces it.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:24.840
I dunno, she was interviewed on 60 minutes
and she said that over the summer, 300 different

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:31.820
Donald Trump ads were not approved and they
were not run at all because they violated

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.420
either YouTube or Google's guidelines.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:40.979
And immediately as news started to spread
of this, speculation was rampant about if

00:01:40.979 --> 00:01:46.230
Trump's ridiculous ads are mostly allowed
on YouTube.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:51.080
What was in the ones that were so bad that
YouTube rejected them?

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:55.830
CBS reviewed the documents and realized we
have no idea why they were rejected.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.500
We see that they were rejected, but we don't
know why.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:02.560
Could it be because the lads were telling
extreme lies or inaccuracies.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.920
Could it be that the titles had bad punctuation
or grammar?

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.020
Google ads don't allow stuff, for example,
like all caps.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:15.530
That's not allowed, but is it just copyright
and I believe that that's the most likely

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:16.530
thing.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.510
There are lots of headlines that are reacting
to this as, wow.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:27.280
YouTube is willing to do what Facebook will
not do, which is not to allow ads that are

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.640
targeted harassment not to allow ads that
are riddled with lies.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:35.650
We have no evidence that that's why these
ads were rejected by Google and YouTube.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:41.530
And the simplest and most likely explanation
is that these ads either had some music in

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:45.710
them that the Trump campaign did not demonstrate
that they had the rights to because I'm sure

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:49.910
they didn't have the rights to it because
Trump regularly uses music at events that

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:54.920
he doesn't have the rights to or that it was
a grammar capitalization, punctuation thing.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.810
That is actually something Google is strict
about.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.709
The lies are not really the problem.

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:04.260
There is no reason right now to think that
YouTube and Google have done anything different

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:08.849
than what Facebook has done about lies in
political ads.

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:09.849
They've done nothing.

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:10.849
Facebook has done nothing.

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:12.550
YouTube, Google has done nothing about it.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:18.819
Susan was just ski, may knowingly be hiding
behind these reports since she knows that

00:03:18.819 --> 00:03:22.629
the reports don't tell us why the 300 ads
were rejected.

00:03:22.629 --> 00:03:27.830
I wouldn't put it past the Trump campaign
to deliberately submit ads they know will

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:28.830
be rejected.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:33.150
So at some later point, they can pull out
of their pockets the victim card and say,

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.310
Oh, our ads are being rejected.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.349
It's anti-Republican bias.

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:39.790
So we've gotta be really careful with these
stories.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:42.480
In case in point, the first headlines were
just wrong.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.459
There was a headline that said, 300 Trump
ads taken down.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:47.870
It's not true.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.530
They weren't approved to begin with.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:52.920
Take down suggests they were public ads.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.470
Something happened, there was outrage and
the ads were pulled.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:57.810
These ads were never approved.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:01.409
And number two, the implication that this
was for content.

00:04:01.409 --> 00:04:02.470
There's not evidence of that.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:06.459
As of right now, most likely this is for copyright
issues.

00:04:06.459 --> 00:04:08.959
Spelling issues, formatting issues.

00:04:08.959 --> 00:04:14.120
If we play along with the false narrative
or at least the unsubstantiated narrative

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:18.989
that these ads were published and then taken
down for content which is not what happened,

00:04:18.989 --> 00:04:24.830
then that allows the Trump administration
to claim martyrdom and to claim anti right-wing

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:25.830
bias.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.409
The reality is they're not the victims here.

00:04:27.409 --> 00:04:31.839
They're most likely benefiting from the power
of the bully pulpit.

00:04:31.839 --> 00:04:36.969
Just like Trump has ignored requests for documents
and testimony and the like without consequence,

00:04:36.969 --> 00:04:42.199
just like Trump regularly flouts the terms
and conditions on Twitter with no repercussions

00:04:42.199 --> 00:04:43.460
whatsoever.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.449
This appears to be another version of the
same thing.

00:04:45.449 --> 00:04:50.300
Let's report what we know happened, which
is simply that ads were not approved.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:55.449
Let's not pretend to know why when we don't,
and I would love to hear by the way from Susan

00:04:55.449 --> 00:05:01.449
was [inaudible] what it is that a YouTube,
if anything, plans to do about inaccurate

00:05:01.449 --> 00:05:06.020
and bullying political ads because we're getting
into the season now and I'll be honest with

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:12.870
you, if YouTube cracks down on inaccurate
or bullying, targeted harassment, political

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:16.129
ads, the David Pakman show will make less
money.

00:05:16.129 --> 00:05:21.930
What I mean by that is election years are
our biggest years historically biggest growth

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:25.069
and biggest what's called revenue per thousand
views.

00:05:25.069 --> 00:05:26.069
Why?

00:05:26.069 --> 00:05:31.210
Because since we do news and politics on YouTube,
more and more candidates start to want to

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:34.280
buy ads that will play before our videos.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:38.229
The way YouTube ads work is that there's a
sort of auction system where when there's

00:05:38.229 --> 00:05:45.419
more demand, you have to be willing to pay
more per time that your ad is displayed because

00:05:45.419 --> 00:05:46.729
there's more competition.

00:05:46.729 --> 00:05:48.080
That price goes up and up and up.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:53.219
When there is a lot of interest in politics,
like in an election year, if indeed YouTube

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:58.369
were to crack down on this, it would be worse
financially for the David Pakman show, but

00:05:58.369 --> 00:06:04.990
it would be the right thing to do because
this has become so toxic and such a reliable

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:11.009
means through which misinformation and disinformation
can be spread that something has to be done.

00:06:11.009 --> 00:06:17.779
However, the practicality of it is extremely
difficult to imagine actually a handling in

00:06:17.779 --> 00:06:22.919
a fair way, which is why I understand Twitter
saying no more political ads.

00:06:22.919 --> 00:06:27.279
I mean, if YouTube did that, we might be out
of business, but I understand why Twitter

00:06:27.279 --> 00:06:29.080
took the decision that they took.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:49.789
Let me know what you think.

